; A macro whose template names something this module IMPORTED, for
; `595-macro-imported-ambiguous.ax` and
; `596-macro-capture-in-module.ax`.
;
; `dup` resolves here to `AmbB`'s, and that is what the macro means
; wherever it is invoked. An entry file that imports `AmbA` as well
; makes the name ambiguous, and one that binds `dup` at the
; invocation would capture it - one refusal each.
(import AmbB)

(pub macro (useDup v) (dup v))
